# Line endings: text is stored and checked out with LF for everyone, whatever their
# core.autocrlf setting. Several tests read source files as text and match multi-line
# strings (passenger-app/__tests__/App.test.tsx), and Prettier expects LF, so a CRLF
# checkout on Windows breaks them. See docs/decisions/0003-line-endings.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one text type that genuinely needs CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never convert binaries, even if they look like text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.3mf binary
*.stl binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
*.gguf binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
